### CreatorAi Auth API — HTTP examples (Phase 2)
### Base: http://localhost:4000/api/v1
### Docs: SDD.md §5.1 + §5.10; Development Plan Phase 2
###
### Variables (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client):
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@email = phase2.tester@example.com
@password = password123
@name = Phase Two Tester
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### ============================================================
### 1) REGISTER — happy path
### Expected: 201 (or 200) with user public fields + JWT
### ============================================================
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "{{name}}"
}

### ============================================================
### 2) LOGIN — happy path
### Expected: 200 with token (+ user / workspace ids)
### ============================================================
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### ============================================================
### 3) ME — happy path (Bearer token)
### Expected: 200 with current user (no passwordHash)
### ============================================================
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================
### 4) LOGOUT — client discard (optional server blacklist)
### Expected: 204 or 200; client must drop token regardless
### ============================================================
# @name logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================
### NEGATIVE CASES
### ============================================================

### 5) Duplicate email on register
### Expected: 409 (or 400) with error.code e.g. EMAIL_TAKEN / CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Duplicate Attempt"
}

### 6) Login with wrong password
### Expected: 401 with error.code e.g. INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrong-password!!"
}

### 7) Login with unknown email
### Expected: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (do not reveal whether email exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 8) ME without Authorization header
### Expected: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 9) ME with malformed / garbage token
### Expected: 401 UNAUTHORIZED / INVALID_TOKEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.jwt

### 10) Register validation — password too short (< 8)
### Expected: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "short.pw@example.com",
  "password": "short",
  "name": "Too Short"
}

### 11) Register validation — missing fields
### Expected: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "missing.fields@example.com"
}

### 12) Register validation — invalid email
### Expected: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Bad Email"
}
